      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Auburn%2C_Wyoming"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The first settlement at Auburn was established in 1879 by permanent settlers moving into the valley.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Auburn%2C_Wyoming"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Pioneer farmers and ranchers surveyed the Auburn townsite into twenty-four ten acre blocks in the spring of 1888.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://starvalleywy.com/city/Auburn/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Old Auburn Rock Church, one of the oldest buildings in Star Valley, was erected in 1889.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26,
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://starvalleywy.com/city/Auburn/"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Old Rock Church once served as a place of worship for Latter-Day Saints and a community meeting place.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://starvalleywy.com/city/Auburn/"
    },
    {
